\[ Version 202607 ]

## try - break - continue - return

# break and continue

When a *try* block is inside of a loop, *break* and *continue* can not be
used.

Nevertheless *break* and *continue* work when the loop is inside of a *try*
block. They also work ever inside *catch* blocks.

# return

Fixed return inside of nested *try* blocks.
